5da01fa7c"],"m":108},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_109","t":"First up! The one concept that I absolutely love (while identifying the QM@D is easier for me than identifying QM@S) I dont know if its the color? I feel like its almost stupid for me to even think that.\n\nEITHER WAY! Here is my first QM.","a":"HoyPip12","d":"","n":"#109","p":5,"im":["a7693c2fa6561aba23ee23ac73f6b32091b069f2"],"m":109},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_110","t":"06 OF 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#110","p":5,"im":["9f27b76aae854a721c44ce1b455e813dbaed4fbd"],"m":110},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_111","t":"That's a nice QM there. What I don't see is whether it's at HTF Supply. This is always important, and shouldn't be overlooked","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#111","p":5,"im":[],"m":111},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_112","t":"07 OF 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#112","p":5,"im":["7c6c6010d25dce06b34a8f55899950cd9991f069"],"m":112},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_113","t":"hornet wrote: Could this be a QM in the making?\n\n05 of 20\n\nI haven't looked at the bigger picture on Bund, but could This be a QM in the making?","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#113","p":5,"im":["1b47654b50e8076b88525afdfb3c2443f0be7718"],"m":113},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_114","t":"Hi bushido, nice to see your commitment, but there are mixed stuff into your homework that need to be cleared. If you have clearly understood the dynamics behind the price you can go even whit \"crappy shape qm\", but please, if you have to post this stuff here add even an explainetioni for the healty of less experienced people; otherwise if those are supposed to be textbook qm well..some are not. some example in chart. hope make sense, keep in posting:)>-","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#114","p":5,"im":["ef0bacea05f2c96cca64f5c5a7fe2a96dd9317aa","41d09e65d982719b06ea166eb641ae4f2236a8b9","8e56f9442230c4ad0b4744653419085f0c97bcfc"],"m":114},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_115","t":"Ifmyante wrote: I haven't looked at the bigger picture on Bund, but could This be a QM in the making?\n\nbigger picture shows resistance swapped support just below, around the 139.00 area. I guess you're right, seeing a QM off support for possible move up.","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#115","p":5,"im":["f923bc506bb89663d56bf3ffb0496b6915c681f7"],"m":115},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_116","t":"Regards whiteout!\n\nI will post comment on how did I make the levels:\n\nExample 21: at L point - price was immediately rejected of the level with blue bar which closed lower then the HL level was closed with red bars\n\nExample 20: attached, on lower time frames the price didn't closed/opened at the same levels for creating QM pattern - so when we are checking this kind of levels we take decisions on current TF or lower ones what concernes the closing/opening of the price?\n\nExample 15: checked, you have right, my mistake\n\nThanks for the comments - from the past cases of different behaviour of the price in different charts - on my opinion - all the levels are not always to the pinpoint exact -even to some 1s chart.\n\nSome of them are not textbook - that's why I also posted to open a discussion on it -very pleased for your comments and also for any future ones from other people.\n\nMistake: difference is measured between HH and LH.\n\nMakes sense - certainly:)","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#116","p":5,"im":["358cc925eb1f18310752736679243e3e18b993c9"],"m":116},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_117","t":"Is this a QM?\n\nPlease ignore the \"price remembered\" comment it's from another post:)","a":"Simon","d":"","n":"#117","p":5,"im":["9e34eae3dbaa7f6b1d2f7d245824b0db03ef9f37"],"m":117},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_118","t":"100 % qm in h1 demand","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#118","p":5,"im":[],"m":118},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_119","t":"Traded this one.","a":"HoyPip12","d":"","n":"#119","p":5,"im":["85439171471a1eb6372685108713a27e041a186a"],"m":119},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_120","t":"Background","a":"HoyPip12","d":"","n":"#120","p":5,"im":["6f836bbba486cf82a506b8df73211acd6b3a2229"],"m":120},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_121","t":"","a":"jkrick33","d":"","n":"#121","p":5,"im":["3afb80fcc22eb0692bf0571a89033ad28e868d45"],"m":121},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_122","t":"We look for QMs at HTF Supply and Demand.\n\nHere's the anatomy of an ideal one They're not always exactly like this one, but can all be easily explained using the ideas of S and D\n\nA QM doesn't need to form all at once either Here's a video of one which took many months to form - it was also one of my favourite trades ever\n\nHomework:\n\nFind at least 20 QMs through history and file them. They can be in any TF, any pair. Find ones that worked, and ones that failed. You'll learn from both","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#122","p":5,"im":[],"m":122},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_123","t":"Hi everyone,\n\nI'm wondering if this is a valid presentation of a QM?\n\nAn area of interest is the lower righthand shoulder. Would we have waited this one out and not been filled? Or maybe because price didn't actually reach the lower shoulder and pocket of new demand this is not a QM?\n\nPlease excuse the sloping dashed white line. It seems to help with eye training.","a":"Simon","d":"","n":"#123","p":5,"im":["ef926105af6b42622aea5bf64ca0c067223438ed"],"m":123},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_124","t":"M1 QM into H4 Supply.","a":"Simon","d":"","n":"#124","p":5,"im":["ac4b93ee3fe9c380eee9ab309da917e33a8abf6d"],"m":124},{"id":"quasimodo_p5_125","t":"Hello!\n\nMy opinion after checking your chart below:\n\n- the right H isn't in the same or lower line of price like the left one (starting of QM) - also the wicks are not so long - should be more obvious that there is rejection of the price at that level\n\nThe teachers will tell - but I wouldn't consider this as valid QM.","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#125","p":5,"im":[],"m":125}],"images":[{"k":"43db7652ce0e79df9ae0025022b3dc9d0beb3653","t":"assets/thumbs/43db7652ce0e79df9ae0025022b3dc9d0beb3653.webp","f":"assets/images/43db7652ce0e79df9ae0025022b3dc9d0beb3653.jpeg","w":1500,"h":846,"b":56498,"o":"43db7652ce0e79df9ae0025022b3dc9d0beb3653.jpeg","p":5,"pid":"quasimodo_p5_1